-- title:
--   Dominated approximation of cubically integrable functions
-- statement:
--   For every $f\in L^3(\mathbb R^2;\mathbb C)$ there are continuous compactly supported functions $g_n$ and an integrable $D\ge0$ such that, for almost every $z$,
--   $$
--   |g_n(z)|^3\le D(z)\ \text{for all }n\qquad\text{and}\qquad g_n(z)\to f(z).
--   $$
--
--   Continuous compactly supported functions approximate $L^3$ functions almost everywhere, under a single cubic domination. This is the form needed to pass estimates from nice functions to all of $L^3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/CubicApprox.lean#L41-L76

